  "configuration_id": "config_010",
  "reason": "We have multimodal (config_011: 0.5362) and rna_only (config_008: 0.5203) baselines, but no image_only baseline. This leaves a critical uncertainty: is the ~1.6% multimodal gain due to genuinely complementary information, or simply from added model capacity? config_010 (image_only, singleprofile, resnet50, no aggregation, no fusion) is the cleanest single-variable comparison to config_008, matching profile setting, aggregation, and fusion while swapping modality. It uses the same resnet50 encoder as config_011, enabling a direct three-way decomposition (RNA vs image vs both). Under a tight budget, resolving whether the image modality contributes independent signal is the highest-priority question, as it determines whether all downstream fusion, aggregation, and multiprofile experiments are worth pursuing or whether RNA-centric designs should be prioritized."
}

